<article class="prose-view">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-body-secondary">Last updated: {{updated}}</p>
{{#unless ads}}
    <p><strong>In short:</strong> Wayhop has no accounts, uses no cookies or analytics, and doesn't track you.</p>
{{/unless}}
{{#if ads}}
    <p><strong>In short:</strong> Wayhop has no accounts or analytics and doesn't track you itself. It shows ads from Google, which uses cookies as described under <a href="#advertising">Advertising</a>.</p>
{{/if}}

    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Your language</strong> (English or Greek), saved in your browser so pages open in it next time.</li>
        <li><strong>The last three metro stations you picked,</strong> so the subway planner can offer them first next time.</li>
        <li><strong>The metro stations you starred as favourites,</strong> so the subway planner offers them before any other.</li>
        <li><strong>Whether you chose the light or the dark colours,</strong> if you did, so the pages open in them.</li>
        <li><strong>Copies of pages and timetables,</strong> saved by the app so it works offline.</li>
        <li><strong>Your location,</strong> if you allow it: your browser uses it to find the bus stops and metro station nearest to you. The last one is kept on your device for 10 minutes, so the next page can use it straight away, even without a signal. It isn't sent to Wayhop's server.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can clear all of this in your browser's settings for this site.</p>

    <h2>What reaches our server</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>The bus stops you're looking at.</strong> To show live arrivals, the bus page asks the server for nearby stops by their number. Those stops are near you, so they show roughly where you are, but they aren't kept with anything that identifies you. Arrivals are kept per stop for a few minutes and shared by everyone.</li>
        <li><strong>Your IP address, for one minute.</strong> To share OASA's live data fairly, the server counts each address's requests for new stops over one minute, in memory only.</li>
        <li><strong>Standard web server logs.</strong> Like any website, our host's web server logs each request (IP address, page, time and browser) for security and to fix problems.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Wayhop's server, not your device, asks OASA for live data, and those requests carry only the stop number.</p>

{{#if ads}}
    <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
    <p>To cover its costs, Wayhop shows a few ads from Google AdSense. They're always labelled "Advertisement", come after the page's content, and are never placed in live arrivals or route results.</p>
    <p>Google and its partners use cookies and similar technologies to show ads, measure them and prevent fraud, and, if you agree, to personalise them. In the European Union, Google asks for your choice before using cookies for ads. If you don't agree, you may still see ads that aren't personalised.</p>
    <p><button type="button" id="ad-choices" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary rounded-pill" data-ad-client="{{adClient}}" hidden>Change your ad choices</button></p>
    <ul>
        <li>{{#external href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"}}How Google uses information from sites that use its services{{/external}}</li>
        <li>{{#external href="https://myadcenter.google.com/"}}Google's ad settings{{/external}}, to turn off personalised ads</li>
    </ul>

{{/if}}
    <h2>Other websites</h2>
    <p>Walking directions open Google Maps, and announcements link to the OASA and STASY websites. Their own privacy policies apply there.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you and ask us to delete it. Wayhop keeps almost nothing that identifies you, but <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with any question. You can also complain to the {{#external href="https://www.dpa.gr/"}}Hellenic Data Protection Authority{{/external}}.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
{{#unless ads}}
    <p>If anything here changes, for example if Wayhop starts showing ads, this page will say so first.</p>
{{/unless}}
{{#if ads}}
    <p>If anything here changes, this page will say so first.</p>
{{/if}}
</article>
